Grand Façade was invoked by [[Mr. Wilder]] in [[Hernán Cortés' vault]] to fight against [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] [[Caliban]] for the [[Ring]] of [[Umbra]], the [[Legendary Titan]] of Dimensions. After a big fight, Grand Façade was defeated when Dante trapped his legs using [[Stopglue]], allowing Caliban to find and stab Grand Façade's unarmored back. {{Source|The Power of Umbra}}

Grand Façade again was invoked by Mr. Wilder in [[the Professor's castle]] in a fight for [[Rassimov|Rassimov's]] secret files. After throwing [[Cherit]] against a wall, he attempted to attack [[Den Fears]] before being hit by Cherit's energy blast. He then tried to asphyxiate [[Grier]] who responded by invoking [[Breaker|Powerbonded Breaker]]. Grand Façade was then defeated when Breaker used his Crushing Grip power on him. {{Source|An Ally from the Organization}}

Mr. Wilder later invoked Grand Façade in Yonaguni, whilst fighting the Huntik team for the [[Amulet]] of [[Kyojin]]. Lok tried to attack him with the [[Willblade]] but Grand Façade deflected the attack, redirecting it at [[Sophie]] and Den, rendering them unconscious. He then joined [[Myrmidon]] in fighting [[Pendragon|Powerbonded Pendragon]]. When Lok managed to retrieve the Amulet, he summoned Kyojin, causing a huge whirlpool, knocking everyone backwards and sending Grand Façade and the Organization underwater. {{source|The Guardian of Yonaguni}}

*Grand Façade's summoning command is "'''Show them'''."
*The name "Grand Façade" uses the English variant spelling of the word "facade," making him the only Titan whose official English name is spelt with an accent (a cedilla), as seen in ''[[Huntik Magazine]]''. {{Source|HM18}} 
**Due to localized captioning guidelines that often ommit accents on letters, Netflix subtitles spell Grand Façade's name without the cedilla as ''Grand Facade''.
